# Deliberately un-ignores this directory's .env, whatever the repo root says.
#
# The root .gitignore keeps having `.env` / `*.env` appended to it by tooling —
# five times now — and because the last matching pattern wins, a negation in
# the root file cannot survive the next append. A .gitignore in a SUBDIRECTORY
# takes precedence over a parent's for files under it, so this is the one place
# the rule holds.
#
# It has to hold because the Emergent deploy image is built from the repo: an
# ignored backend/.env ships a container with a stale environment, which is
# exactly how live Razorpay keys went missing in production three times
# ("Authentication failed", "Couldn't start checkout · HTTP 502").
# Guarded by tests/test_pay_health.py::test_env_files_are_not_git_ignored.
!.env
